## Goal
Make `install` leave exactly one registered Portero.app (DEV-46: stale copies hijacking links), and address review findings on PR #13: safer swap, safer build, correct default-handler status, robust install tests.

## Problems
- Codex cross-review found another `lsregister` dump form: the `(0x0-0x...)` record suffix. Without handling it, an old copy could stay registered.
- A version string with `/`, `&` or similar broke the sed substitution and produced an invalid `Info.plist` (an unescaped ampersand). Escaping in sed was fragile.
- Install tests had to run on a machine with an older `build/` directory and off macOS.

## Decision
- `scripts/install.sh` copies the new app to `Portero.app.new`, removes the old one, then moves the new one into place. If the copy fails, the old app stays. A failed enumeration now exits 1 instead of reporting "no other copies".
- `scripts/build-app.sh` validates `VERSION` up front and accepts only letters, digits and `. _ + -`. Rejecting unsafe input is simpler and safer than escaping it for sed and XML.
- `cmd/portero/app.go`: the default-status report compares the two scheme handlers as the same file, and `lsreg.Others` returns scanner errors.
- `scripts/test-install.sh` skips off macOS and tolerates an old `build/`.
- Security review (subagent) approved, Claude Code Review passed.

## Rejected
- Escaping `/`, `&`, `|` and backslash in the sed replacement: it still produced an invalid plist for `&`, and it is more brittle than validation.

